{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1034155-scelesti-rules-in-signs-of-sorcery","id":1034155,"title":"Scelesti Rules in Signs of Sorcery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-18T12:02:10-08:00","id":1034155,"title":"Scelesti Rules in Signs of Sorcery?","content":"In this post, Dave mentions that 2E rules for these guys are coming:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971278#post971278\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971278#post971278\"> Abyssal Imago - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971278#post971278\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971278#post971278 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How does this work exactly? Do I just add on X points to the Reach cost of a spell? Do I get to actually use it for something, IE Advanced Duration? If so, what stops a player from using exactly as much reach as they need to for the spell they want, and saying that reach was the 'Extra' reach the condition requires? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Two of my favorite mage characters (one retired) are Scelesti, using hacked rules I've thrown together from Left-Hand Path / Tinkering. I'd love to see the official stuff for these two. Has anything been mentioned about <i>where</i> or <i>when</i> these rules are coming? Maybe in the new supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:10:10-08:00","id":1034161,"title":"","content":"A detailed outline of Signs of Sorcery was given <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">in this post</a>. While it doesn't mention Scelesti, it might cover the 'corrosive addictiveness' and 'befouling a spell,' based on the chapter devoted to the Mage's Tools.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to these rule updates myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:49:14-08:00","id":1034258,"title":"","content":"It's been ten months since that post. It might've changed since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"